(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_zoology_biotechnologyanditsapplications=[{id:"neet-2026-q156",pn:156,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biotechnology and its Applications",st:"Bt toxin genes",q:"The toxin proteins isolated from Bacillus thuringiensis, coded by which of the following genes would control cotton bollworms and corn borer, respectively?",o:["cryIAc and cryIIIAb","cryIAc and cryIIAb","cryIAc and cryIAb","cryIIAb and cryIAc"],c:2,s:`Bt toxin genes were isolated from Bacillus thuringiensis and put into crop plants such as cotton.
The choice of gene depends on the crop and the target pest, as most Bt toxins are specific to an insect group.
The toxin is coded by a gene named cry.
The proteins coded by cryIAc and cryIIAb control cotton bollworms, and the one coded by cryIAb controls corn borer.
So cryIAc for cotton bollworms and cryIAb for corn borer, which is option 3.`},{id:"neet-2026-q162",pn:162,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biotechnology and its Applications",st:"Transgenic animals: products",q:"The human protein named \u03B1-1-antitrypsin, obtained from transgenic animals, is used for the treatment of ____ .",o:["Alzheimer's disease","Emphysema","Rheumatoid arthritis","Cystic fibrosis"],c:1,s:`The correct answer is option 2.
The human protein \u03B1-1-antitrypsin, obtained from transgenic animals, is used to treat emphysema.
Transgenic models also exist for the study of other diseases such as Alzheimer's disease, rheumatoid arthritis and cystic fibrosis.`},{id:"neet-2025-q144",pn:144,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Biotechnology and its Applications",st:"RNA interference",q:"Silencing of specific mRNA is possible via RNAi because of",o:["Complementary dsRNA","Inhibitory ssRNA","Complementary tRNA","Non-complementary ssRNA"],c:0,s:`RNAi (RNA interference) takes place in all eukaryotic organisms as a method of cellular defence.
It silences a specific mRNA because of a complementary dsRNA molecule.
This dsRNA binds to the mRNA and prevents its translation.`}]})();
